  "summary": "Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list is ready under RBC-RAD-07. Four studies are booked. Three cancelled appointments (pt-0048, pt-0012, pt-0050) are not on the list, so I placed no orders for them.\n\n1. pt-0047 Mohr, 08:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with IV contrast (sr-t0001). No contrast allergy. Has diabetes, and his last creatinine (9/24) was more than 30 days ago, so I ordered a creatinine to be drawn before the scan (sr-t0009). Outside labs that arrived while I worked show creatinine 1.04 → 1.52 within 24 h, which counts as AKI. So I kept the pre-scan creatinine and added 0.9% NaCl 500 mL IV at 07:00 (mr-t0021). He's not on metformin. Sent instructions, then a corrected message (comm-t0011, comm-t0025). Follow-up task for the AKI (task-t0032).\n\n2. pt-0015 Ferreira, 09:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with IV contrast (sr-t0002). His allergy list says \"anaphylaxis\", but the radiology report from the day (2019) graded the reaction to iohexol as moderate. So he gets premedication: prednisone 50 mg at 20:00 Sunday, 02:00 and 08:00 Monday (mr-t0005), and diphenhydramine 50 mg at 08:00 (mr-t0006). He needs a driver. While I worked, a corrected creatinine arrived: 2.8 (eGFR ≈ 24). The 0.98 first reported was another patient's sample. I added NaCl 500 mL IV at 08:00 (mr-t0020). Sent instructions in Spanish and English, then a correction (comm-t0012, comm-t0026). Follow-up task for his kidney function (task-t0033).\n\n3. pt-0049 Schuster, 13:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with IV contrast (sr-t0003). She had AKI at the ED on 10/4–10/5 and her creatinine hasn't been documented back to baseline. I ordered a creatinine drawn before the scan (sr-t0010) and NaCl 500 mL IV at 12:00 (mr-t0007). Her metformin is on hold (mr-00392): none on the scan day or for 48 h after, and restart only once a recheck is normal (task-t0015). An outside report that arrived while I worked shows a moderate reaction to iopamidol in 2022. So I added prednisone 50 mg at 00:00, 06:00 and 12:00 (mr-t0022) and diphenhydramine 50 mg at 12:00 (mr-t0023). She needs a driver. Sent instructions and an update (comm-t0013, comm-t0027). I couldn't add iopamidol to her allergy list because I couldn't confirm a code for it, so that still needs doing.\n\n4. pt-0046 Beahan, 14:00, CT abdomen/pelvis without contrast, stone protocol (sr-t0004). No contrast, so no prep, and I told her so (comm-t0014). An outside record shows a mild reaction to iohexol; I added it to her allergy list (alg-t0024). Her order and instructions didn't change.\n\nI wrote notes and addenda in each chart and closed the four new inbox items with links to the orders and messages. The older items in your inbox are about other patients and are still open.",
